      "text": "The equation of an ellipse with center at $(h, k)$ is $\\frac{(x-h)^2}{a^2}+\\frac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1$, where $a>b$.  Our ellipse therefore has the equation $\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1$.  Its foci are located at $(\\pm 3, 0)$, and its minor axis is contained within the x-axis; we call the foci $F_1$ and $F_2$, where $F_1= (3,0)$.\nWe see that $F_1$ is also a center of a circle with no part of the\ncircle being outside the ellipse.  The endpoints of the minor axis of the ellipse, $(-4, 0)$ and $(4, 0)$, are both at a distance of 4 from each focus.  These points are also a distance of 4 from the center of the circle, $F_1$.  Hence,\nthe radius of the circle is 4.",
